  "traps": [
    "Exhibit A sheet has a merged title row and a blank row above the real header row (row 3); the header must be found, not assumed to be row 1.",
    "TOTAL row (Gross 2,220,646, Cleanable 1,450,645, Fixtures 1176) is not a facility; per Addendum Q4 it also includes information-only rows.",
    "Building # mixes text with leading zeros (\"0012\", stored as text) and plain numbers (1102, stored as numeric cells).",
    "Building 0030 Ballman Speer has 0 service days and Remarks \"Storage – no custodial service\": excluded from expected facilities.",
    "Building 0084 Hawthorne Hall is a normal-looking row in the workbook (5 days/week) but Addendum No. 1 Q3 in the PDF removes it from scope: excluded.",
    "Building 2210 Nursing and Allied Health shows 48,210 GSF in the workbook; Addendum No. 1 Q2 corrects it to 42,810 (cleanable 36,400 unchanged). Truth uses 42,810.",
    "Building 1114 Ridgeview Commons exists only in the PDF addendum (Q1): 11,000 GSF, 9,350 cleanable, 1 floor, 14 fixtures, 7 days/week. It must be added to the workbook buildings.",
    "Cleanable SF is far below gross for residence halls (common areas only), warehouse/shops (office areas only) and the Aviation Technology Center (hangar bays excluded) — gross and cleanable must not be swapped or averaged.",
    "Service Days/Week is a number: 5 = daily_5, 7 = daily_7, 3 = 3x_week, 2 = 2x_week, 1 = weekly; 6 (Mon–Sat) has no exact service level so truth omits serviceLevel for those rows; 0 = not serviced.",
    "Remarks column carries free text (APPA Level 1 notes, exclusions) that must not leak into numbers; the Notes sheet is free text with numbered notes, not building rows.",
    "Sycamore Suites and Juniper/Cedar Hall have identical or large gross SF but different cleanable SF; Juniper and Cedar Hall are twin buildings with identical numbers (98,450 / 29,540) and must both be kept (different building numbers).",
    "Prior award: total contract value $14,950,000 over five years (60 months) with incumbent, contract number and award year in Section 3; the Q5 FTE count (118 custodial FTEs, 9 supervisors) is staffing context, not contract value.",
    "Contract term: one-year initial term plus four one-year renewals = 5 contract years."
  ]
}
